    <DataNode elementId="CPDQT-280" textLabel="glucoraphanin" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="GMMLNKINDDUDCF-BYNGITTOSA-M" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="500" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco">The hydrolysis of the 4-methylsulfinylbutyl glucosinolate |FRAME: CPDQT-280| by |FRAME: EC-3.2.1.147|, leads to the production of the isothiocyanate |FRAME: CPD-19494|, which is a major inducer of phase II detoxification enzymes that are important in chemoprotection from carcinogens |CITS: [9294217]|. Broccoli contains a non-functional allele of |FRAME: EC-1.14.11.M8| and thus accumulates large amounts of |FRAME: CPDQT-280| |CITS: [12671761]|.</Comment>
